From: Pat Wendorf <dungeons@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] locker: no lock for sleep when the session logged in automatically

The locker locks on every logind PrepareForSleep, with no setting to
turn that off, so a machine set to log in without a password still asks
for one on every wake. Skip the sleep lock when /etc/pengyos/autologin.conf
names this session's user, and release the delay inhibitor so the sleep
goes ahead. Locking by hand (Super+Escape, loginctl lock-session) is
unchanged, and turning automatic login off brings the sleep lock back at
the next sleep.

Upstream: no lock-on-suspend option on cosmic-greeter master (2026-10-24)
---
diff --git a/src/logind.rs b/src/logind.rs
index 74da8e4..b779ffe 100644
--- a/src/logind.rs
+++ b/src/logind.rs
@@ -84,6 +84,29 @@ pub fn subscription() -> Subscription<Message> {
     })
 }
 
+/// PengyOS: the account that logs in automatically, from
+/// /etc/pengyos/autologin.conf (GDM's custom.conf format, written by
+/// `pengyos-autologin` and AccountsService). Read the way greetd-config reads
+/// it: the last AutomaticLoginEnable and AutomaticLogin lines win, and root
+/// never counts. Read at every sleep, so turning automatic login off brings
+/// the lock back at once. An unreadable file means "lock".
+fn autologin_user() -> Option<String> {
+    let conf = std::fs::read_to_string("/etc/pengyos/autologin.conf").ok()?;
+    let value = |key: &str| {
+        conf.lines()
+            .filter_map(|line| {
+                let (k, v) = line.split_once('=')?;
+                (k.trim() == key).then(|| v.trim().to_string())
+            })
+            .last()
+    };
+    match value("AutomaticLoginEnable")?.as_str() {
+        "True" | "true" | "1" | "Yes" | "yes" => {}
+        _ => return None,
+    }
+    value("AutomaticLogin").filter(|u| !u.is_empty() && u != "root")
+}
